The removed `InternalCalls.InvokeJS<T0,T1,T2,TRes>` is marked with the comment "This method only exists for backwards compatibility... The exact namespace, type, and method name must match the corresponding entries in driver.c in the Mono distribution." The PR removes it without showing that no supported runtime still depends on it. Nothing in this repo calls it, so the rest of the build will be fine. The risk is at runtime, when an older Mono/WASM runtime looks for that export.

This should be confirmed with the runtime owners before merge, and the PR description should say so.

